{{!--
  Pathfinder 2e — the generic card, front.

    front-title    the name, in the shared header over the red rule
    front-body     the card's text as markdown, the whole of the content

  The furniture of every other front — the header, the footer with the
  source and the English original — around a body that has no structure
  of its own: running text, `###` sub-headings, lists, tables and
  pictures, written as markdown in the note itself. The body is one
  place, and the card type says what fills it, in order: `content` in
  the block, a `## Vorderseite` section, and failing both the note's own
  text before its first heading. Open a note, write the card.

  The author steers the pagination: what must stay together goes between
  `%% keep-together %%` and `%% /keep-together %%`, a hard break is
  `%% card-break %%`. Both are Obsidian comments, invisible in the note.
--}}
<div class="card-root card-front pf2e generic-card">
  {{> header}}

  <div class="card-content-container">
    <div class="card-body-scalable">

    {{#if (slot "front-body")}}
    <div class="pf2e-flavor pf2e-generic-body">{{slot "front-body" markdown="block"}}</div>
    {{/if}}

    </div>
  </div>

  {{> footer}}
</div>
